From: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: select valid link for unspecified TX link

Group addressed frames reach ath12k_mac_op_tx() with no STA and with the
TX control link field set to IEEE80211_LINK_UNSPECIFIED, so
ath12k_mac_get_tx_link() falls back to ahvif->deflink.link_id.

deflink is preallocated storage that is reused for whichever link of an
ML VIF comes up first, and ath12k_mac_unassign_link_vif() memsets it when
that link goes away. Its link_id is then zero while the remaining links
keep their own ids, so the fallback selects link zero. On a VIF whose
links do not include link zero, for example an MLD covering only 5 GHz
and 6 GHz, ahvif->link[0] is NULL and every such frame is warned about
and dropped.

Select the first driver-backed active link instead. The set of live links
is the only valid source for this decision; deflink.link_id describes a
storage slot, not a link. Intersect active_links with links_map so frames
are not redirected to links which are being removed, and keep the
existing fallback when no active driver link remains.

The link zero case handled here is reached through the unspecified link
field, which the check added in 113-wifi-ath12k-select-valid-link-when-
link-zero-is-missing.patch does not cover as it matches an explicit zero
in the TX control field.

Fixes: 648a121bafa3 ("wifi: ath12k: ath12k_mac_op_tx(): MLO support")
Signed-off-by: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -9578,12 +9578,17 @@ u8 ath12k_mac_get_tx_link(struct ieee802
 	struct ieee80211_link_sta *link_sta;
 	struct ieee80211_bss_conf *bss_conf;
 	struct ath12k_sta *ahsta;
+	unsigned long links_map;
 
 	/* Use the link id passed or the default vif link */
 	if (!sta) {
 		if (link != IEEE80211_LINK_UNSPECIFIED)
 			return link;
 
+		links_map = vif->active_links & ahvif->links_map;
+		if (links_map)
+			return __ffs(links_map);
+
 		return ahvif->deflink.link_id;
 	}
 
